githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":69,"state":"open","created_at":"2012-09-12T10:39:14Z","updated_at":"2019-04-22T10:38:08Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2014-12-14T07:17:23Z","updated_at":"2014-12-19T22:57:19Z","closed_at":"2014-12-19T22:57:19Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In 0.9.6.1, when `faceforward` is used with a vector type, it results in the following error under Visual Studio 2015:\n\n```\nerror C2677: binary '<': no global operator found which takes type 'glm::tvec2<float,0>' (or there is no acceptable conversion)\n```\n\nThis seems to be because `dot` returns a scalar, which is then compared to a vector.  For example, the instantiation of `faceforward<vec2>` is equivalent to:\n\n```\nvec2 faceforward(vec2 const & N, vec2 const & I, vec2 const & Nref) {\n    return dot(Nref, I) < static_cast<vec2>(0) ? N : -N;\n}\n```\n\nAdding a `faceforward` specialization for vector types in `func_geometric.inl` fixes this error.  The key difference being, we need to cast `0` to `T` instead of `genType`:\n\n```\ntemplate <typename T, precision P, template <typename, precision> class vecType>\nGLM_FUNC_QUALIFIER vecType<T, P> faceforward(vecType<T, P> const & N, vecType<T, P> const & I, vecType<T, P> const & Nref)\n{\n    return dot(Nref, I) < static_cast<T>(0) ? N : -N;\n}\n```\n\nPerhaps there may be a more succinct solution if there is something like the following already implemented (I don't know GLM internals well enough to know)\n\n```\ntemplate <typename genType>\nstruct GetValueType {\n    typedef genType value_type;\n};\ntemplate <typename T, precision P, template <typename, precision> class vecType>\nstruct GetValueType<vecType<T, P>> {\n    typedef T value_type;\n};\n```\n\nIn which case the existing `faceforward` implementation can simply be changed to use `static_cast<typename GetValueType<genType>::value_type>(0)`.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/289/reacti